LIBRESSL
========

Original source can be downloaded from:
https://ftp.openbsd.org/pub/OpenBSD/LibreSSL/

file   = libressl-4.3.4.tar.gz
size   = 9311161
sha256 = 57c8b2f8c6f9505587abaeddab003ea243d615edb7ed71957968121fc6316bd6

The file README.DELETED contains a list of deleted files and directories:
the autotools and CMake build files, the tests, the compat sources the
system does not need (all but crypto/compat/syslog_r.c) and the files for
Windows, MinGW and macOS.

These sources are used in:
	lib/librecrypto		libprivate_crypto.so.57
	lib/libressl		libprivate_ssl.so.60
	usr.bin/openssl
	usr.bin/nc		(with the libtls sources built in)

Local modifications (git log crypto/libressl shows them):
	crypto/chacha/chacha-merged.c		__bounded__ for compilers other
						than OpenBSD's
	include/openssl/md5.h			no <stddef.h> or opensslconf.h
						under _KERNEL
	include/openssl/opensslfeatures.h	OPENSSL_NO_HW_PADLOCK

The portable LibreSSL's include/compat headers are kept and used: they
provide pledge, unveil, syslog_r, timespecsub and the like, according to
the HAVE_* settings in lib/librecrypto/Makefile.inc.

The source lists in lib/librecrypto/Makefile, lib/libressl/Makefile,
usr.bin/openssl/Makefile and usr.bin/nc/Makefile, and the HAVE_* and
assembly settings, are what LibreSSL's own configure produces for an
x86_64 DragonFly target (the libc's functions; the x86_64 ELF assembly).
To regenerate them on a Linux host with tools/linux/build.sh tools done:

	PATH=$OBJDIR/host/bin:$PATH ./configure \
	    --host=x86_64-unknown-freebsd14 --build=x86_64-pc-linux-gnu \
	    CC=xcc --enable-nc ac_cv_header_dlfcn_h=no ac_cv_lib_dl_dlopen=no

(DragonFly is not in LibreSSL's list of hosts; freebsd gives the ELF
x86_64 assembly.)  Then print libcrypto_la_SOURCES, libcompat_la_SOURCES
and the CPPFLAGS from crypto/Makefile, libssl_la_SOURCES and
libbs_la_SOURCES from ssl/Makefile, libtls_la_SOURCES from tls/Makefile,
openssl_SOURCES and nc_SOURCES from apps/*/Makefile, and DEFS.  The
compat arc4random sources it lists are left out: libc has arc4random.
